    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "Đong Kirgnign\nDONG KINGMAN\nMIAMI",
      "Cocktaiko\nSherry\nDubonnet Campari\nManhattan Gin Martini Vodka Martini\nVermouth\nBloody Mary Screwdriver Whiskey Sour\nTom Collins Vodka Collins Daiquiri Scotch Bourbon\nCanadian Gin Vodka Rum\nPremium Beer\nMenus\nAperitivo\nApéritif\nDelicia Florida\nLush crabmeat and ripe melon with an orange curry dressing.\nFilet Mignon Maitre d'Hôtel\nSelect grilled tenderloin steak with a savoury herb butter\nPechuga de Ave Smitane\nTender breast of chicken in a peppery cream sauce\nPapas Doradas\nArroz Pilaf\nOven browned potatoes\nPilaf rice\nLegumbres en Mantequilla\nButtered vegetable bouquet\nParfait de Helado Tropical\nCoconut and orange ice creams in a tropical taste medley.\nGalletitas Finas\nButter cookies\nCafé\nCoffee\nCafé Descafeinado\nDecaffeinated Coffee\nTé\nTea",
      "paral de helado tropical\nCoconut and orange ice creams in a tropical taste medley.\nCafe\nCoffee\nGalletitas Finas\nButter cookies\nCafé Descafeinado\nDecaffeinated Coffee\nTe\nTea\nSelected Red and White Wines\nChampagne Brut\nDrambuie Bénédictine Creme de Menthe\nCognac Napoléon Contreau\nKahlúa\nAmaretto di Saronno\n323 KS",
      "MIAMI\nDong Kingman, the award winning Chinese-American artist, travels the world sketching and painting the beautiful,\nthe monumental and the picturesque. His watercolors grace more than forty\npermanent museum and private collections in the USA and abroad\nHere he depicts Miami, city of glitter and glamour, of sun and sand, of gleaming highrise hotels and condominiums.\nHost to millions who come for the pleasure of basking amid palms and flowers in this the hub of tropical South Florida.\nOne of the most renowned playgrounds in the world, Miami offers a variety of recreation. From golf and tennis to\ndeepsea fishing and yachting. From thoroughbred racing to the \"Son et Lumière\" presentations at exquisite Vizcava.\nMiami also serves as gateway to the Caribbean Cruise World. From here luxury liners offer frequent sailings in\nconjunction with Pan Am's \"Air-Sea\" Flights.\nPan Am jets land at Miami's busy International Airport from all major cities on its US network, from Central and\nSouth America and key European cities such as London, Paris and Frankfurt.\nPAN AM.\n2001.080.235"
    ],
